# Keep the Isengard project warning-free

Your job is to **fix** warnings in **this** crate (`isengard`), not to hide
them. Leave Cargo’s warning printer alone.

## Do

After any `src/` change, run `cargo check` (or `cargo build` / `cargo run`) and
clear every warning attributed to `isengard` before finishing. Same for
`cargo clippy --all-targets`.

Fix by deleting dead code, wiring APIs into real call sites, or `#[cfg(test)]`
for test-only helpers.

## Do not

- Turn off or filter warning output (`future-incompat-report` frequency,
  `RUSTFLAGS` that hide lints, piping away warnings, etc.).
- Blanket `#[allow(…)]` / `#![allow(warnings)]` to make the build look clean.
  Existing documented allows (e.g. the terminal module) stay; do not add new
  ones to dodge this rule.
- Defer “cleanup warnings later.”

## Out of scope

Warnings that name **other crates** (today: `block v0.1.6` future-incompat from
a dependency) are not Isengard source. Do not chase them on normal tasks, and
do not silence Cargo so they disappear — see [docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md).
